ked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity consistent with a previous biopsy site which is located in the upper inner to central quadrant and communicates with the previously described defect on the posterior margin  The cavity has a smooth to focally nodular  hemorrhagic lining  There is a moderate amount of dense gray white fibrous tissue surrounding the cavity  as well as focal areas of gritty gray white fat necrosis  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  there is a single 1 0cm in greatest dimension possible lymph node identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected  Received in formalin  labeled  right sentinel lymph node biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink portion of soft tissue which is consistent with a lymph node  The specimen is inked black  bisected  and submitted entirely in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Lymph Node  Right sentinel   Excision  report_end  , Positive.
